Both orders of the products of x and g_j⁻¹*x*g_j are collected, for j = 0,1,2.
The cardinality premise makes the collected coordinates unique. Their XOR
differences are the six original equations; square-one is not used. The
selected-conjugate identities remain the explicit CollectedConjugates input.

Generated by
GroupTests/IdentityPairs/source/generate.py; each certificate is kernel-checked.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith A.3.12, pp.47–48; the unchanged literal PC relations.
-/

